otengine/godot/issues/comments/2925886644/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":1,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3069303640","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/104458#issuecomment-3069303640","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/104458","id":3069303640,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc628dtY","user":{"login":"adamscott","id":270928,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI3MDkyOA==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/270928?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/adamscott","html_url":"https://github.com/adamscott","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/adamscott/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/adamscott/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/adamscott/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/adamscott/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/adamscott/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/adamscott/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/adamscott/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/adamscott/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/adamscott/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-07-14T12:27:39Z","updated_at":"2025-07-14T12:27:39Z","body":"FYI @marcosc90, [I suggested in the \\#web channel of the Godot Developers Chat](https://chat.godotengine.org/channel/web?msg=xdGYZxuBLMPqPi9hw) that we revert this PR for the time being, at least for 4.5. Unfortunately, it seems that the current implementation makes the default Web editor build fail to actually run, because of a deadlock (see #108484).\r\n\r\nIt seems that by some miracle, the fact that the Godot thread pool was only running on a single thread, it made so that every thread spawned by the editor could in fact be spawned without creating a deadlock. By setting Godot thread pool count to 4 by default, well the deadlock happens.\r\n\r\nI worry that games could suffer the same way, and there's not really another way than cranking up the number of Emscripten thread pool count, or setting the number to 1.\r\n\r\nThe other reason is that there's no way currently to determine these numbers like case by case. It could be nice to be able to set the Godot thread pool count to 1 or very low if `navigation.hardwareConcurrency` is very low, and high vice versa. And the ability to set a number of emscripten threads relative to the hardware concurrency reported by the browser.\r\n\r\n> Most browsers have a hard cap on threads, historically, that cap has been quite low.\r\n> When hardware concurrency is capped the value of `navigator.hardwareConcurrency` [may be the cap](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/API/Navigator/hardwareConcurrency#value) (**may**, i.e. `hardwareConcurrency` may in fact be more than the cap).\r\n> This means we can't trust too much the value of `navigator.hardwareConcurrency`.\r\n\r\n@Faless I did a little experiment, and from what I gathered so far, it doesn't seem that there's an hard cap (anymore?). We can spawn a number of threads times higher than `navigator.hardwareConcurrency`. So having a emscripten thread pool high count (just as a precaution) could be interesting. Here's my experiment: https://codepen.io/adamscott/pen/wBKavjN","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3069303640/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]